request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere. --behaviour

governor turn 1: plan -> commands  (The only failure comes from my own acceptance test, which wrongly asked list() to hide completed todos by default. The request didn't ask for that, and the transcript shows the default list has always included completed items. The rename itself works: tsc passes and the saved todos.json uses "completed". This replaces the acceptance test with one that checks the rename without changing behaviour.)
round 1: owners commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc exits 0 and all 13 vitest tests pass, including the acceptance test. The manifest shows Todo now has completed: boolean and no done field. The CLI transcript shows the saved JSON uses "completed", and the list output is unchanged ('[x] walk dog'). ListOptions.includeDone is an option name rather than the Todo field, so it was left as it is to keep the interface stable.)

